    "sentence_translations": [
      "True Listening Ability",
      "",
      "Today was the English exam.",
      "",
      "After the exam, Little Qiang asked Little Ming: “Little Ming, how did the exam go?”",
      "",
      "Little Ming said: “I couldn't understand anything of the listening comprehension.”",
      "",
      "Little Qiang didn't believe him, and asked: “So what did you write? Did you guess everything?”",
      "",
      "Little Ming said: “Our class' top student in English, Xiao Xiao, was sitting behind me.”",
      "“She makes a lot of sound when she writes, so I listened to her.”",
      "",
      "Little Qiang still didn't understand, and asked:",
      "“If she didn't tell you the answer, how could you know if she wrote A, B, C or D?”",
      "",
      "Little Ming laughed and said:",
      "“I listened to the strokes! ‘A’ has three strokes, and you must write three lines, so it will sound three times.”",
      "“C has one stroke, so it makes 1 sound.”",
      "“B and D both have two strokes, and make two sounds, but D is written a bit faster.”",
      "",
      "Little Qiang was dumbfounded: “Is that even possible?!”"
    ]
